# Johannesberg vegetation control file.
#
# 2026-11-08 -- the inner 2,048 m frontier now carries the REVIEWED generation of
# review-2026-11-08 (vegetation/review-2026-11-08/README.md), published through the
# compiler's reviewed-candidates import (compile-vegetation.mjs --reviewed), not by the
# machine-v1 chain this file used to drive. OWNER DECISIONS of 2026-11-08, recorded here
# and in the review README:
#   1. Publish although the workflow's 90% precision/recall gate is not met on the unseen
#      held-out sample (round 2: P 0.953, R 0.788). The shortfall is closed stands
#      (touching spruces in the 2021 leaf-off scan, 17/23), a data limit; isolated trees,
#      groups and broadleaves meet or approach the gate. Holds and unresolved cases stay
#      listed in the review.
#   2. Use the ROUND-2 (type-aware) detector -- a post-evaluation owner choice for fewer
#      false trees on open ground, not the declared F1 ranking (round 1 F1 0.869 vs 0.863).
#   3. Every placed tree stands on its own detected crown; 'near' trees (zone A of a hole
#      line or practice area) and 'woodland' trees are both individual records, woodland
#      ones thinned by id at low quality; only canopy no crown claims is topped up as a
#      stand field.
#   4. Owner species check (same day): the first publication typed 24% of the records near
#      play broadleaf, many of them shaded or edge conifers. A broadleaf call now needs a clearly
#      leafless April 2021 crown (vegetated share below 0.2); between that and the conifer call
#      the type is unknown and the runtime's background mix chooses. See the review README,
#      "Species check".
# The 192 outer finest tiles keep the 2026-09-11 machine-v1 records and stands byte for byte.
#
# A machine-v1 publish from this file would REPLACE the reviewed inner generation with
# re-detected trees, so publish stays false: re-run the inner ring only through the
# reviewed import (tools/johannesberg-tree-pilot + compile-vegetation.mjs --reviewed).
publish=false
